Arcanum CE patch 1 of 3 for innospect 0.2.0 (gogx, 2026-10-31).

A chunk whose data entry lacks ChunkCompressed is stored, whatever the
installer's compression method; innospect decoded every chunk with the
installer's method. innoextract decides it in setup/data.cpp. Without it
GOG's Arcanum 1.0.7.4 installer fails on 191 of 317 entries with
"invalid LZMA2 dictionary property 120". Review finding E1:
arcanum-work audits/review-20261031-innospect.

--- a/src/extract/chunk.rs
+++ b/src/extract/chunk.rs
@@ -103,6 +103,14 @@
     // For encrypted chunks, an EncryptionContext is required.
     // Without one, surface `Error::Encrypted` so the caller can
     // react (typically by re-parsing with a candidate password).
+    // Arcanum CE patch (gogx, 2026-10-31): a chunk without ChunkCompressed
+    // is stored, whatever the installer's method, as innoextract decides in
+    // setup/data.cpp. GOG's installers store their .dat archives this way.
+    let compression = if data.flags.contains(&DataFlag::ChunkCompressed) {
+        compression
+    } else {
+        CompressMethod::Stored
+    };
     let chunk_is_encrypted = data.flags.contains(&DataFlag::ChunkEncrypted);
     if chunk_is_encrypted && encryption.is_none() {
         return Err(Error::Encrypted);
